I think for me uh more recently this  label of being a covered dissident has  come from my U-turn if you like or I  would more likely want to describe it as  evolution in my understanding of the  benefits and harms of the covid-19  vaccine specifically the MRNA vaccine to  the Pfizer moderna vaccines  um and I was actually one of the public  advocates  very early on in the pandemic  um when the vaccine rollout started in  in December of 2020 January 2021  I was one of the first to take two doses  of the fisa vaccine  and a month later I was actually on Good  Morning Britain  trying to help tackle uh in a  compassionate way vaccine hesitancy  which was particularly prevalent amongst  the ethnic minority communities in the  UK and I know that's similar in the US  because I convinced a friend of mine  who's a well-known film director called  garinda cheddar well known for movies  like Bend It Like Beckham Blinded By the  Light which is on Bruce Springsteen  um she was receiving a lot of what at  the time I felt was in quotes  um anti-vax misinformation through blogs  and asked me around  um whether or not she should take the  vaccine and I I said to her listen  vaccines and I still believe this to be  the case in traditional vaccines  certainly uh one of the most safest  pharmacological interventions in the  history of medicine so I didn't in any  way shape or form even conceive of the  possibility  of any vaccine causing significant harm  let alone the covered vaccines  but over a period of around a year Brett  um  my  um opinion changed quite significantly  because of a number of different events  um probably the first that made me think  about it was my father who was a retired  doctor  um the honorary vice president of the  British Medical Association very  well-known doctor he suffered  um a unexplained and unexpected sudden  cardiac death in July of 2021.  um I was actually involved in the whole  uh in the events leading up to his death  because he'd called me  um he was suffering from chest pain  which sounded cardiac I was in London he  was in Manchester so a couple hundred  miles away  and we were on the phone and in between  our phone calls he suffered a cardiac  arrest which was witnessed by  two of his neighbors were doctors and  despite the fact that they uh carried  out CPR immediately and ambulance was  called there was a delay in the  ambulance Etc and I was down the line so  it was quite a harrowing experience for  me but  um and of course he was also on a  personal level I was very very close to  him he was my best friend I knew his  lifestyle habits inside out he was the  last surviving member of my immediate  family so I had a quite a profound  effect on me but  um because of the fact that he was  otherwise well and I knew his cardiac  history which was non-significant  um I I asked for a post-mortem to be  carried out  and it's post-mortem findings were quite  shocking he had two critical or severe  stenosis or narrowings in three out of  three of the major arteries two of them  were severely narrowed and um that would  suggest certainly compared to scans I'd  organized a few years earlier just  routine stuff they had a rapid  acceleration of of his blockages so you  know my area of interest and research a  lot of my advocacy over the years Brett  has been on changing the understanding  of our heart disease develops but also  what can be done to even potentially  Halt and even reverse heart disease  that's you know I've published on this  stuff extensively you may be aware of  that work so if anybody had has  expertise in understanding this it's me  and it didn't make sense and the only  thing I could attribute it at the time  my only explanation which again didn't  fully fit but I thought well you know  you have to think about all the  possibilities was my father under very  profound severe psychological stress  that caused an acceleration of his  Coronado disease  um and then a few months later  a number of different bits of data  emerged  um which for me started to put a picture  together to suggest that the MRNA  vaccines could be  um that a major cause behind my dad's  death and of course many other uh  unexpected cardiac arrests and heart  attacks and that was first and foremost  there was an abstract published in  circulation by Stephen gundry which  suggested that the MRNA vaccines were  causing huge coronary inflammation  through inflammatory markers that would  increase cardiovascular risk very  rapidly  um at the same time a colleague  from a very prestigious British  institution I won't name name that  institution  um to protect his uh identity but he  basically said that um researchers at  his institution had accidentally found  by use of coronary Imaging that the  vaccinated versus unvaccinated were  having huge  um increases in uh coronary inflammation  as well  having found this they decided they had  a closed meeting that they were not  going to publish these findings because  they were worried about  the fact that they may lose funding from  the pharmaceutical industry and then  only a few weeks earlier I had been  contacted by a journalist for the Times  newspaper and actually given an  interview  where she said that there was reports  from hospitals in Scotland of a uh  unexplained rise in heart attacks about  25 increased risk and heart attacks  which were not associated with covid and  asked me what was the cause of that now  before I'd become familiar with these  potential harms from the vaccine I had  again attributed it to  maybe the knock-on effect of lockdowns  poor diet and stress because actually  the major factors normally in the  development of heart disease 80 of heart  diseases is lifestyle related are issues  such as poor diet sanitary lifestyle  poor sleep and and chronic psychological  stress so I had predicted there probably  would be a signal anyway coming in the  next few years even when the pandemic  started from those factors and I still  think they probably play a role  um but then I decided Brett after all of  this to  um first and foremost as a my duty as a  doctor and because I have a public  profile I went on GB news which is a  news channel over here and I said that  you know I'm concerned there may be a  significant link here between the MRNA  vaccines and heart heart attacks and it  needs investigating  um that video went viral  um I had to put up behind the scenes  many people don't know this but after  that um I had a couple of very uh um  let's put it this way a medical  organizations linked to my medical  license and my affiliation my  postgraduate um credentials essentially  contact me because of complaints that  were made by Anonymous doctors I was  promoting you know anti-vaxx information  Etc so I had to deal with that in the  meantime over a few weeks and that  luckily didn't end in any specific  censorship  um but I then decided what I needed to  do really to open this up is to spend my  time  critically appraising the data  thoroughly and then publishing it in a  medical journal and I did this over a  period of nine months and as you  probably know  um a few weeks ago I published these two  papers in the Journal of incident  resistance where I had concluded  um unequivocally based upon the evidence  that the um the MRNA vaccines need to be  suspended uh pending an inquiry because  the signal of harm is significant and  it's based upon very high quality  evidence now  it is a long answer and there are quite  a number of things I want to return to  in there but I think first and foremost  let me just say  um that's a terrible story about your  father and uh I'm you have my  condolences and I'm sure my audience is  properly shocked by  um what must have been uh  uh at a terrible  realization not only of his passing but  of the possibility that  um your profession had been involved in  some way in advancing a therapy that had  this terrible terrible consequence so  anyway thank you Brad and then on that  note the irony of this is my father  obviously it had two doses of the  vaccine early on he had actually  convinced me because I realized I knew I  was low risk from covert and I'm sure we  can talk about that a bit later but  um he had really convinced me  emotionally because you know he had lost  his wife my mother a few years ago just  to get into the human side of it and I  think that he like many people who are  older had a a very I would say  exaggerated fear of covid  and for him obviously I'm his you know  only surviving son  um and uh he you know he was worried  about me and he said listen please you  know and actually one of the main  reasons I had it was because I didn't I  didn't necessarily need to have it so  quickly I could have waited it's because  of him uh and also as somebody that was  the honorary vice president of BMA and  he also was a prolific writer he did a  lot of media work he was a very strong  Advocate again for the vaccine as well  so that's also you know they're they're  thrown into the picture which  complicates the situation  yeah it sure does I I will say  um I also received pressure from people  who loved me and wanted me to get  vaccinated  um and in in fact at the beginning of  the vaccination campaign I thought I  would I was pretty excited about the  vaccines  [Music]
 

